PHASE 2 — MOCK TRADING AUDIT
Complete Trade Lifecycle

1. Signal arrives (from research API or engine signals endpoint)
   Source: /api/mock-trading/signals or /api/strategy-signal-trace
   ↓
2. scoreMockTraceRow() / scoreMockResearchSignal()
   signal_score + threshold_bonus(50 max) + quality_score×0.15 + mtf_score×0.10
   ↓
3. evaluateMockTradeOpenRisk()  ← PRIMARY REJECTION FUNNEL
   (mockTradingEngine.ts lines 573–645)
   ↓
4. mockTradingEngine.openPosition()
   - Entry price ± slippage (5 bps)
   - Fee deducted (0.05% taker)
   - Position stored in MockAccountState
   ↓
5. Per-tick evaluation: evaluateMockExits()
   - SL crossed → close STOP_LOSS
   - TP crossed → close TAKE_PROFIT
   - Age > maxHoldMinutes → close MAX_HOLD
   ↓
6. closePosition()
   - Exit slippage applied
   - Exit fee deducted
   - PnL computed
   - MockRejectionEvent or MockTradeEvent emitted
   ↓
7. computeAnalytics() / computeVerdict()
   - Strategy aggregate updated
   - Research edge score recalculated
   - MongoDB persist via /api/mock-trading/trades
Rejection Reason Analysis — Ranked by Blocking Impact
Rank	Rejection Reason	Default Threshold	Why It's a Blocker	Estimated % of Signals Blocked
1	NO_APPROVED_STRATEGY	Strategy must have ≥12 trades + PROMOTE verdict	Cold-start blocker. Zero trades means zero promotions. A new deployment blocks 100% of signals until the research tournament runs enough cycles.	95–100% at cold start
2	LOW_SIGNAL_SCORE	minSignalScore = 50	Signal scoring formula depends on quality_score and mtf_score which may not be populated by all signal sources. If sources emit only signal_score, threshold bonus is the only additive component.	30–60% ongoing
3	EXPOSURE_LIMIT	maxOpenTrades = 5, maxLong = 3, maxShort = 3	At 5 open positions all new signals blocked. With 15-min cooldowns and 45-min holds, accounts can stay full for hours.	20–40% when active
4	COOLDOWN	15 minutes per strategy	With 100+ strategies at 1m timeframe, high-frequency strategies refire every candle. 15-min lockout means 15 candles rejected per fired strategy.	15–30% ongoing
5	REGIME	Market regime classifier	If regime = NO_TRADE (ranging, high vol), all signals blocked regardless of score. BTC spends ~40% of time ranging.	20–40% regime-dependent
6	CONFIRM	Multi-timeframe alignment gate	If higher-timeframe confirmation is not aligned, signal dies here. MTF data availability may be unreliable.	15–25%
7	ATR_FEES	ATR must exceed fee hurdle	In low-volatility periods (BTC ATR < 0.15%), fee hurdle is never met. This blocks entire low-vol sessions.	10–30% volatility-dependent
8	RR_TOO_LOW	Minimum R:R = 1.5	Strategies with fixed SL/TP geometry near this boundary will cluster rejections here.	10–20%
9	DAILY_LOSS_LIMIT	3% of starting equity ($30k on $1M)	Once hit, entire session blocked until midnight. Any bad day kills the rest of the day.	100% when triggered
10	FAMILY_CONFLICT	Opposite direction open in same family	With 100+ strategies in ~10 families, mixed-direction signals are likely on every choppy candle.	10–15%
11	DUPLICATE_POSITION	1 open position per strategy ID	Prevents scaling into winners. With 100+ strategies competing for 5 slots, this fires frequently.	5–15%
12	LOW_CONFIDENCE	Below confidence threshold	Generally caught earlier by signal score gate. Secondary filter.	5–10%
13	WEEKLY_LOSS_LIMIT	6% of starting equity	Rare unless consecutive bad days.	<5%
14	MARGIN_CHECK	Insufficient simulated margin	With $1M simulated and 25x leverage, margin is rarely the issue.	<2%
15	MAX_DRAWDOWN	10% historical drawdown	Triggered after sustained losses. Rare unless system is failing.	<2%
16	OTHER	Catch-all	Diagnostic. Should be zero.	Unknown
Why the System Most Likely Fails to Generate Trades:
The combination of NO_APPROVED_STRATEGY (cold-start) + REGIME (40% of market time) + LOW_SIGNAL_SCORE (scoring formula gaps) creates a scenario where a fresh deployment with no promoted strategies can run for days without a single fill. The minSignalScore = 50 threshold is also never calibrated against the actual distribution of incoming scores — it is a hardcoded constant.

